 which he all expected  however he says that the m2 is actually  gonna be based on the three nanometer  process and from the list it says tsmc  ff3 and it's actually going to be the  first custom arm v9 processor from apple  however he says that we are actually  getting one more chip that's going to be  coming out this year it's going to be  apparently  another one that's kind of based on the  m1 which he thinks it could be something  with the m1x or some kind of other name  and apparently it's coming with the same  updated avalanche and blizzard cores  that we already have on the a15 which is  very disappointing now the crazy thing  about this leak from trim apple pro is  that this actually matches up to  something that ming chico talked about  because ming said that this year for the  iphones only the pro models are getting  the a16 while the regular 14 and 14 max  are getting the a15 both with six gigs  of ram however the difference is the new  a16 will have lp ddr5 memory which is  exactly what shrimp apple pro said and  if you think about it if they're both  based on the n5p process it kind of  makes sense why apple would have both of  these chips a15 and a16 available across  the entire iphone 14 lineup because in  reality they're not that different and  this actually leads me to an even more  important point because a couple of  months ago minchiko actually mentioned  that the macbook air could get a  modified version of the m1 chip and that  the m2 chip would be delayed which is  literally exactly what shrimp apple pro  just confirmed he said we should be  getting another kind of m1 based chip  this year with the real true m2 being  delayed until next year which is crazy  because i didn't believe ming chi kuo  when he made this leak a couple months  ago march 8th saying that it's gonna  have an m1 chip processor no mini led  display a new redesign and more color  options i couldn't believe it but now it  kind of actually makes sense if this new  chip is actually based on n5p but going  even deeper chance miller who is the  editor-in-chief at 95 mac said that quo  told him that it could be a modified  version of the existing m1 and that the  actual m2 could be pushed to 2023 which  perfectly matches up to what shrimp  apple pro is saying but here is the main  detail he says really it just comes down  to marketing names and we all know  apple's history there because apple  could call it whatever they want to  because if you remember the 2020 ipad  pro they said it comes with the a12 z  chip well in reality it was literally  the exact same a12x chip from the 2018  ipad pro except with one extra gpu core  enabled and that allowed them to call it  the a12z which is just pure marketing so  here's my crazy little theory about  shrimp apple pro's new leak what if this  final soc of the m1 family of chips is  actually going to be modified and called  the m2 because apple could call it  whatever they want and they could just  delay the real m2 and then call that the  m3 and ik dave made a very good point he  said apple could easily just call a chip  with avalanche and blizzard cores the m2  and then the three nanometer one the m3  and same thing with serenby saying to be  honest apple could easily just brand  this as the m2 chip even if the upgrades  are minor and then here was my take on  that no matter what it actually becomes  it must be named the m2 because apple  did say that the m1 ultra was the last  chip in the m1 family they said that at  their last march 8th event so whatever  they do with the ship no matter how  minor it is no matter if it's mainly  based on the same n5p process this new  chip needs a new name and guess what  shrimp apple pro just added to his leak  this morning he says now my source  agreed that this new m1x chip the  modified version could be the m2 instead  yes officially in terms of marketing it  could just be modified and they could  call it the m2 with four avalanche four  blizzard and then 10 a