ase scenario that i  had for the m2 which is basically that  is based on the a15 instead of a newer  generation third nanometer and this is  exactly what nine to five mac  leaked with an exclusive leak saying  that the m2 chip is known as statin and  it's based on the current a15 which i  really hoped wouldn't happen because i  was hoping it would be based on a future  a 16 instead so before i get into the  actual performance numbers and charts  that we should expect for the m2 chip i  want to explain why i think apple  decided to stick to n5p  for the m2 chip well first of all  samsung's four nanometer which is  basically the third gen five nanometer  has horrible yields for qualcomm  snapdragon 8 gen 1 ship apparently they  were so bad they were only 35  in terms of yield which means that if  they made 100 chips they would only keep  35 and they would throw away the rest of  them which is absolutely horrible and  apparently tsmc actually had better  results where they would get a yield  rate of over 70 percent and that's why  they're going to be used for the  snapdragon 8 gen 1 plus but even then if  you make 100 chips you still have to  throw away around 30 of them which could  be why apple decided not to go for third  gen 5 nanometer because they might be  trying to save as much money as possible  because the yields for five nanometer or  the first and second gen are amazing way  back in 2019 they reported yields of  over 80  which was already very impressive and  then a year after that in august of 2020  they said that their yields got even  better with yields of around 90  and now two years later i'm sure they're  probably sitting at around 94 95 based  on their own estimates so maybe that's  why apple chose to stick around to n5p  once again and this finally brings us to  the performance this is actually a video  right here that i made around five  months ago with two different scenarios  one scenario is that the m2 chip would  be based on the a15 which i really  didn't want to happen and the other one  is it would be based on the a16 and now  it looks like it is gonna be based on  the worst case scenario a 15 so let me  show you guys the performance that we  should expect first of all in terms of  single core cpu performance instead of  around 17 14 points for the m1 the  second gen m2 chip should be around 1876  which honestly isn't that big of a  difference because with the scenario two  it would be over 2 000 which would be  awesome but unfortunately it looks like  that is not gonna happen and then moving  on to multi-core this is actually a  little bit of a better improvement  because instead of around 7400 the m2  chip based on the a15 should be around  8700 which is a little bit better but  the biggest difference we should expect  is actually in terms of the gpu as you  can see instead of getting around 21 000  points with the m1 the m2 chip should  get around 28 800 even though it's based  on the a15 and that's because we are  expecting two more gpu cores yes up to a  10 core gpu with the m2 so that's going  to be a big improvement right there so  with all that said it looks like the m2  chip is not going to be as good as we  thought it would be but it's still going  to be a decent improvement so hopefully  apple gives us some extra features and  changes with the actual mac itself to  make it more enticing maybe with like  wi-fi 6e bluetooth 5.2 in other new  features because it looks like the  performance difference is not going to  be that huge so if you disagree with my  thoughts on this video then comment them  down below but if you enjoyed it click  the circle above to subscribe for more  videos like this one definitely check  out one of those two right there thanks  for watching and we'll see you in the  next video  [Music]

